! si16-1k-ecut30.in as a magnetic noncollinear spinor run without symmetry, 3x2x1 grid:
! 6 k-points with the spinor sizes of a magnetic spin-orbit run, for pool scaling.
! Silicon, sixteen atoms, at a production cutoff.
!
! Twice si8-1k.in again -- 64 electrons, 32 bands -- in a tetragonal cell with
! c/a = 2. Still the same crystal, so the energy per atom is known from the
! smaller cells and any disagreement is this code's fault rather than the
! system's. This is the size at which the cost is genuinely dominated by the
! physics rather than by fixed overheads, which is what makes it the useful
! case to optimise against.
 &control
    outdir = './tmp', prefix = 'si16-spinor-6k',
    calculation = 'scf'
 /
 &system
    ibrav=6, celldm(1) =10.20, celldm(3) =2.0,
    nat=16, ntyp=1,
    ecutwfc=30.0,
    noncolin = .true., nosym = .true., noinv = .true.,
    starting_magnetization(1) = 0.5, angle1(1) = 45.0, angle2(1) = 30.0
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-10
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086  Si.pz-vbc.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS crystal
 Si  0.00000  0.00000  0.00000
 Si  0.00000  0.50000  0.25000
 Si  0.50000  0.00000  0.25000
 Si  0.50000  0.50000  0.00000
 Si  0.25000  0.25000  0.12500
 Si  0.25000  0.75000  0.37500
 Si  0.75000  0.25000  0.37500
 Si  0.75000  0.75000  0.12500
 Si  0.00000  0.00000  0.50000
 Si  0.00000  0.50000  0.75000
 Si  0.50000  0.00000  0.75000
 Si  0.50000  0.50000  0.50000
 Si  0.25000  0.25000  0.62500
 Si  0.25000  0.75000  0.87500
 Si  0.75000  0.25000  0.87500
 Si  0.75000  0.75000  0.62500
K_POINTS automatic
 3 2 1 0 0 0
